  "verified": true,
  "evidence": "All 20 verdicts Shay Green's spc_smp and spc_mem_access_times reach agree with values taken on a console, and gilyon's spctest, which tests every opcode but SLEEP and STOP, reports Success. Peter Lemon's seven SPC700 cartridges print every PASS their source prints with one field excused: the status words they compare differ from their expectations in the interrupt flag alone, which this processor leaves set after a reset.",
  "howToSettleIt": "Settled for what Shay Green's and gilyon's cartridges reach. Peter Lemon's expected values carry no stated hardware provenance, so they leave what a reset puts in the interrupt flag open; divergences.json records it, and OPEN-QUESTIONS.md carries it under what the part holds when it comes up.",
